#
# SGLang v0.5.21 + our SM121 build patches. Created 2026-10-03 to track the
# v0.5.21 line (released 2026-10-02, tag e00930c548, 784 commits since v0.5.20).
# NOT BUILT YET: no acceptance-gate run, no GPU/serving run. Every PATCH VERIFY
# line below is host-side against raw v0.5.21 source, never against a built
# image.
#
# THE HEADLINE: the build side is quiet once more. Nothing that feeds a recipe
# knob moved except the cosmetic sgl-kernel patch suffix. Torch, flashinfer,
# transformers, kernels, cutlass-dsl, tokenizers, sglang-kernel, sgl-deep-gemm,
# compressed-tensors, tilelang and the sgl-kernel tree location are all pinned
# to the same values as v0.5.20. What moves in python/pyproject.toml:
#   * xgrammar==0.2.1 -> ==0.2.7 (#39026, XGrammar V4.1 DSML constraints)
#   * sentencepiece (unpinned) -> ==0.2.1 (0.2.2 rejects null pieces in InternVL
#     tokenizers, cherry-pick #41788)
#   * NEW dependency "regex" (unpinned)
#   * diffusion extra: cache-dit 1.3.0 -> 1.5.1; test extra: sgl-eval 0.1.0 ->
#     0.1.2 (neither is installed by this recipe's flow beyond missing_deps
#     --extra diffusion, see OPEN RISK H)
# And on the kernel side: #40033 moved the CUDA/ROCm speculative kernels
# (eagle_utils, ngram_utils, packbit, speculative_sampling) from the AOT
# sgl-kernel build to JIT, so the AOT SOURCES list lost four entries.
#
# TODO(release-review): v0.5.21 breaking-changes review and SM12x redundancy
# check (what upstream absorbed that we carry by hand) is being done in
# parallel and will be merged here. Until then see OPEN RISK C / F below, which
# are still the v0.5.20 texts and NOT re-checked against this ref.
#
# ── DELTA vs sglang-0.5.20-sm121.recipe ─────────────────────────────────────
#   1. SGLANG_VERSION 0.5.20 to 0.5.21, SGLANG_REF to v0.5.21.
#   2. SGL_KERNEL_PATCH_VARIANT "-v0.5.20" to "-v0.5.21". COSMETIC again: the
#      four patch BODIES are byte-identical to the -v0.5.20 ones, only the @@
#      line numbers of skip-sm90-target (all 4 hunks) and skip-flashmla move,
#      by -4, because #40033 deleted four csrc/speculative/*.cu entries from
#      the CMakeLists SOURCES list. See the NOT-A-TRIPWIRE note in PATCH VERIFY.
#   3. FLASHINFER_VERSION UNCHANGED at 0.6.18.post1. v0.5.21 still pins
#      flashinfer_python[cu13]==0.6.18 (pyproject.toml:42). Do NOT reach for
#      0.7.0, it is outside the ref's pin.
#   4. BASE_IMAGE / TRANSFORMERS / KERNELS / CUTLASS_DSL / HF_HUB / TOKENIZERS /
#      AUDIO / ACCELERATE / SGL_KERNEL_DIR / TILELANG_PATCH_VARIANT: ALL
#      UNCHANGED. v0.5.21 still pins torch==2.13.0 (torchaudio 2.11.0),
#      transformers==5.12.1, kernels>=0.14.1,<0.15, nvidia-cutlass-dsl[cu13]==
#      4.6.2, tokenizers==0.22.2, sglang-kernel==0.4.7, sgl-deep-gemm==0.2.0,
#      sgl-deep-ep==0.1.2, tilelang==0.1.12, compressed-tensors==0.18.0,
#      quack-kernels==0.6.4, cuda-tile==1.6.0rc5, apache-tvm-ffi==0.1.11,
#      humming-kernels[cu13]==0.1.12, smg-grpc-servicer>=0.9.0.
#   5. Every APPLY_* flag keeps its v0.5.20 value; the reasons are re-verified
#      against this ref in PATCH VERIFY below, not carried over.
#   6. Upstream dependency churn that rides along with the ref (informational,
#      none of it a knob here). aarch64 wheels verified on PyPI 2026-10-03:
#      xgrammar-0.2.7-cp312-cp312-manylinux_2_26_aarch64, sentencepiece-0.2.1-
#      cp312-cp312-manylinux_2_27_aarch64, regex-2026.9.29-cp312-cp312-
#      manylinux2014_aarch64. nvshmem4py-cu13 is still unpinned upstream and
#      now resolves to 0.4.0 (cp312 manylinux2014_aarch64 wheel exists; was
#      0.3.1 last cycle). Upstream's own docker/Dockerfile only bumped
#      MSCCLPP_VERSION to sglang-v0.10.1 and a GDRCopy libgdrapi glob; we build
#      from scitrera's Dockerfile.sglang-nightly, so neither applies.
#
# ── PATCH VERIFY (2026-10-03, host-side, against raw v0.5.21 source) ─────────
#   OK sgl-kernel-arch-prune-v0.5.21.patch        regenerated, content identical
#   OK sgl-kernel-disable-fa3-v0.5.21.patch       regenerated, content identical
#   OK sgl-kernel-skip-sm90-target-v0.5.21.patch  regenerated, content identical
#   OK sgl-kernel-skip-flashmla-v0.5.21.patch     regenerated, content identical
#      Produced the same way as the -v0.5.20 set: apply in build order
#      (arch-prune, disable-fa3, skip-sm90-target, skip-flashmla), re-diff each
#      step against the previous one, so all four land with ZERO fuzz and ZERO
#      offset (patch -F0). The method was validated first by regenerating the
#      -v0.5.20 set against raw v0.5.20 and getting the four existing files
#      byte for byte. Re-applying the whole set to pristine v0.5.21 reproduces
#      the sequential reference tree and leaves the eight "dgxarley ..." markers
#      in place (arch-prune x2, disable-fa3 x1, skip-sm90-target x4,
#      skip-flashmla x1).
#      NOT A TRIPWIRE, same as v0.5.20: the -v0.5.20 set applies silently on
#      v0.5.21 (all four skip-sm90-target hunks and skip-flashmla at offset -4, no
#      fuzz, resulting CMakeLists byte-identical to the -v0.5.21 set's), and a
#      forgotten suffix therefore builds a CORRECT tree instead of aborting.
#   OK sglang-dsv4-mtp-marlin-v0.5.14.patch       applies (offset 282); still
#      NEEDED: HybridFp8NvFp4Config.get_quant_method in v0.5.21 (modelopt_quant.
#      py:1719-1735) still falls from the nvfp4 is_layer_excluded check straight
#      to Mxfp4FlashinferTrtllmMoEMethod with no marlin branch.
#   OK sglang-tilelang-018-indexer-compat-v0.5.16.patch  applies (offset 46);
#      path python/sglang/kernels/ops/attention/dsa/tilelang_kernel.py unchanged.
#   NO sglang-qwen4exp-pr36497.patch              NATIVE (since v0.5.20), GATED OFF.
#      qwen4_exp.py, qwen4_exp_mtp.py, qwen4_exp_ple_table.py exist in
#      python/sglang/srt/models; a dry-run of the 20k-line patch is rejected.
#   NO sglang-nemotron35-spec-pr36186.patch       MERGED (since v0.5.19), GATED OFF.
#      Dry-run reports "Reversed (or previously applied)".
#   NO sglang-qwen36-mixed-nvfp4-pr27906.patch    MERGED, GATED OFF (same signal).
#   NO sglang-dsv4-nvfp4-pr25820.patch            NATIVE, GATED OFF (same signal).
#   NO sgl-kernel-sm121.patch                     target still gone, GATED OFF.
#      nvfp4_blockwise_moe.cuh exists NOWHERE in the v0.5.21 tree (checked with
#      a full-tree name search; python/sglang/jit_kernel/ itself no longer
#      exists in either v0.5.20 or v0.5.21, the JIT kernels live elsewhere), so
#      NVFP4 MoE keeps running through FlashInfer-CUTLASS.
#   OK Dockerfile chain (2026-10-03): scitrera cuda-containers origin/main is
#      UNCHANGED at 2a3b1b7 (2026-08-21; git fetch origin, nothing new). The
#      patches this recipe enables were dry-run in the script's order against a
#      pristine origin/main container-build tree: dockerfile-sm121, kernels-pin,
#      audio-deps, cutlass-dsl-pin, accelerate, dsv4-flashmla, dsv4-mtp-marlin-
#      tilelang, hf-hub-floor, tokenizers-pin. All apply (sm121 at offset 0, the
#      rest at offsets +8..+97, same as the v0.5.20 chain; no fuzz, no rejects).
#      The other dockerfile-* patches are gated off by this recipe's flags.
#
# ── OPEN RISKS, validate before this recipe is promoted ──────────────────────
#   A. RUNTIME patches (roles/k8s_dgx/files/sglang_patches/): REPLAYED and then
#      RE-ANCHORED 2026-10-03 against v0.5.21. Offline replay is now 0
#      ANCHOR-DRIFT on v0.5.21 AND on the v0.5.20 control, in all FIVE gate
#      scenarios (base, glm, hy3, qwen38 with TP=4, allgates), and idempotent on
#      both (pass 2: nothing patched, gate-skip counts identical to pass 1).
#      The v0.5.20 patched trees are byte-identical to the pre-edit patch set,
#      so every older spelling still works. v0.5.19 was NOT replayed; older
#      pinned images are covered only by the additive/conditional edit shape.
#      NOTE: spark5 was unreachable (powered off), so the harness was rebuilt
#      locally (not the /root/patchreplay-0519 one): fake dist-packages =
#      upstream python/sglang + this recipe's source patches (marlin offset 282,
#      tilelang offset 46, both apply) + the real pinned deps. Dependency pins
#      are UNCHANGED in v0.5.21 (flashinfer 0.6.18, transformers 5.12.1,
#      cutlass-dsl 4.6.2), so the v0.5.20 pins were reused. The scenario set is a
#      reconstruction of replay3.sh's, not a copy. Before the edits the v0.5.20
#      control was clean and v0.5.21 drifted in exactly p10, p37 and p67.
#      WHAT DRIFTED AND WHAT WAS DONE (3 patches):
#        p10 - upstream DELETED multi_thread_safetensors_weights_iterator, so
#              Patch 3 is now conditional on the function existing. Patches 1
#              and 2 (single-thread, buffered) still apply.
#        p67 - ABSORBED. configurer.py now has _sm120_deep_gemm_apis_available()
#              and widens both the probe gate and DEEPGEMM_SCALE_UE8M0 to
#              (120, 121) natively. Self-gated on that helper, so older pinned
#              instances with the env gate on keep both edits.
#        p37 - trtllm_mha part re-ported, PARTIALLY absorbed. Upstream rebuilt
#              forward_extend around uses_native_fp4, which is SM100 GenMHA only
#              (not is_xqa_impl), so SM120/SM121 verify still reads the dequant
#              workspace and the silent word-salad fix is still needed. Native
#              now: removal of the decode-only raise, the KV scale write
#              (*self._kv_write_scales), kv_cache_sf pass-through and the
#              target-verify XQA mask. So the guard and write edits became
#              conditional, the call edit is reduced to supplying the mask for
#              draft-extend-v2, and the FP4 read and bmm-scale edits got a
#              v0.5.21 spelling gated on is_nvfp4_kvcache and is_decode_mode.
#              Hybrid routing and the flashinfer draft-extend fill (parts 1 and
#              3) are unchanged upstream and apply as before.
#      Audited for SILENT absorption and found none: p30/p35 (dsa_indexer
#      changes are ROCm/aiter only, paged_mqa_logits_backend.py unchanged), p34
#      (_forward_trtllm still hardcodes backend="trtllm-gen"), p66 (the QSA
#      _SUPPORTED_HEAD_TOPOLOGIES is still {(12,1),(24,2)}, TP4 widening still
#      needed), p29/p56/p60 (same dep versions, same files). Every other patch
#      injects a byte-identical diff on v0.5.21 and v0.5.20.
#      What the replay still canNOT answer: (1) whether p37's re-ported XQA FP4
#      read, scales and mask give CORRECT speculative output on GB10; run the
#      nvfp4-KV + MTP GSM8K check on the built image, upstream's extend path was
#      rebuilt; (2) whether the modules p30/p35 GENERATE import (the harness
#      reduces write_module's import probe to a syntax check; same known
#      check_generated_imports false positive as v0.5.20); (3) v0.5.21's new
#      --prefill-kv-cache-dequant-dtype, the reworked NVFP4 KV pool (scale
#      buffers may be None) and the layer_boundary/residual_batch model
#      refactors showed no drift but need a boot test.
#   B. INHERITED from v0.5.16, still open: moe_runner_backend cutlass / triton
#      for NVFP4 is gone (#30448), so nvidia/Qwen3.5-397B-A17B-NVFP4 (cutlass)
#      and Minimax-M2.5 @ PP=4 (triton) still need re-testing or re-pinning, and
#      compressed-tensors NVFP4 MoE with apply_router_weight_on_input=True still
#      asserts instead of running. Re-checked: no NVFP4 cutlass_moe_fp4 /
#      nvfp4_blockwise_moe source exists in v0.5.21 either. See TURBOQUANT.md.
#   C. v0.5.21 BREAKING CHANGES:
#      TODO(release-review): fill from the v0.5.21 release notes. The v0.5.20
#      list (SM120 FP8 per-channel route #38006, deleted cutlass_mla / non-Marlin
#      gptq / AWQ AOT dequantize / Dual Chunk FA #32114, --enable-response-store
#      #39122, ...) is already part of the v0.5.20 baseline and is not repeated.
#   D. TORCH: no gap. v0.5.21 still pins torch==2.13.0 (torchaudio 2.11.0),
#      exactly what BASE_IMAGE ships. No new base build for this recipe.
#   E. INHERITED dependency shapes the missing_deps step will try to install:
#      cuda-tile==1.6.0rc5 still has no PyPI wheel for that version (wheel-stub
#      sdist redirecting to pypi.nvidia.com; fix is --extra-index-url
#      https://pypi.nvidia.com, not unpinning). nvshmem4py-cu13 is unpinned
#      upstream (0.4.0 now, aarch64 cp312 wheel exists). missing_deps.py only
#      checks PRESENCE, not version, so a package already installed from the
#      previous layer stays at its old version; see H for the two that matter
#      this cycle.
#   F. SM12x WORK IN v0.5.21 WE HAVE NOT EXERCISED:
#      TODO(release-review): redundancy check of p30/p34/p35 and the other
#      hand-carried SM12x work against upstream additions in v0.5.21. The v0.5.20
#      text (#29927 DeepGEMM paged-MQA on SM120, #30805, #31470) still stands as
#      "check before re-porting runtime anchors".
#   G. INHERITED: NVFP4 ATTENTION on SM121 (flashinfer #3897) is still only
#      KERNEL-level verified (2026-07-28 on spark5), never validated end to end
#      through SGLang with a real uniform-NVFP4 model. flashinfer does not move
#      this cycle (0.6.18.post1 on three refs now), so earlier verdicts are not
#      invalidated by a driver bump. Judge output quality by pattern-grep plus
#      token distribution plus tail, not by finish_reason.
#   H. NEW: version pins that upstream tightened but our image does not honour.
#      scitrera's Dockerfile.sglang-nightly installs `xgrammar` UNPINNED in the
#      "remaining deps" step before missing_deps.py runs, so the image gets
#      PyPI latest (0.2.8 on 2026-10-03), not v0.5.21's ==0.2.7; missing_deps.py
#      then sees it as present and leaves it. Likewise sentencepiece: v0.5.21
#      pins ==0.2.1 because 0.2.2 (current latest) rejects null pieces in
#      InternVL tokenizers; if anything earlier in the build installs it
#      unpinned the image ships 0.2.2. Neither has a recipe knob or a dockerfile
#      patch today (same mechanism as the tokenizers 0.23.0rc0 incident that
#      TOKENIZERS_VERSION guards against). Check
#      `pip list | grep -iE 'xgrammar|sentencepiece'` on the built image; if
#      either deviates, add a pin knob in the style of dockerfile-tokenizers-pin.
#      InternVL is not served here, so sentencepiece is low priority; xgrammar
#      0.2.8 vs 0.2.7 matters only for structured output / tool-call grammars.
#   I. NEW: #40033 moved eagle_utils / ngram_utils / packbit /
#      speculative_sampling to JIT. They are no longer in the AOT wheel we build
#      with arch-prune, so speculative decoding (EAGLE / NEXTN / MTP / ngram,
#      i.e. every speculative profile we run) now compiles those kernels at
#      first use inside the container, for the live GPU arch. Confirm nvcc and
#      headers are present in the runtime image and that the first-launch JIT
#      does not blow the startupProbe budget (SGLANG_CACHE_DIR, see DEPLOY
#      NOTE). Candidate for the acceptance gate.
#
# ── DEPLOY NOTE: SGLANG_CACHE_DIR (#32434, since v0.5.18) ───────────────────
# Triton, FlashInfer, Inductor, DeepGEMM and the CUDA driver cache all live
# under SGLANG_CACHE_DIR, so the FIRST launch on this image recompiles once.
# Setting any of TRITON_CACHE_DIR / FLASHINFER_WORKSPACE_BASE /
# SGLANG_DG_CACHE_DIR / TORCHINDUCTOR_CACHE_DIR / CUDA_CACHE_PATH keeps that one
# where it is. We already set FLASHINFER_WORKSPACE_BASE explicitly in
# roles/k8s_dgx/tasks/sglang_instance.yml, so the expensive flashinfer JIT cache
# is NOT affected; the DeepGEMM cache is, and is the other expensive one.
#
# Prerequisite: xomoxcc/dgx-spark-pytorch-dev:2.13.0-v1-cu132 present on the
# build host (scripts/build_pytorch_base_image.sh, see ensure_base_image_present
# in build_sm121_image.sh). UNCHANGED from v0.5.18 through v0.5.20.
#
DOCKERFILE=Dockerfile.sglang-nightly
TARGET=runtime

# UNCHANGED from the v0.5.20 recipe: v0.5.21 still pins torch==2.13.0
# (torchaudio 2.11.0), so the 2.13.0-v1-cu132 base built 2026-08-28 still
# matches upstream exactly. Do NOT rebuild the base for this recipe.
BASE_IMAGE=xomoxcc/dgx-spark-pytorch-dev:2.13.0-v1-cu132

# flashinfer 0.6.18.post1 - UNCHANGED. v0.5.21 still pins
# flashinfer_python[cu13]==0.6.18 (python/pyproject.toml:42, "keep it aligned
# with jit-cache version in Dockerfile"), so "newest stable inside the ref's
# pin" resolves to the same wheel as the last two cycles. 0.7.0 exists on PyPI
# and is OUTSIDE the pin; do not reach for it to work around a 0.5.21 problem.
# .post1 is 0.6.18 plus exactly one additive cherry-pick (#4931) and a version
# bump; see the v0.5.19 recipe for what 0.6.18 content matters here.
#
# Wheels re-verified 2026-10-03 on https://flashinfer.ai/whl, including the one
# that matters for arm64:
#   flashinfer-jit-cache 0.6.18.post1+cu130 cp39-abi3 manylinux_2_28_aarch64
#   flashinfer-python 0.6.18.post1 py3-none-any
# FLASHINFER_VERSION=0.6.18
FLASHINFER_VERSION=0.6.18.post1

# transformers 5.12.1 - exactly v0.5.21's pyproject pin (==5.12.1, unchanged
# since v0.5.15). Do NOT bump past the SGLang ref (no perf benefit, transformers
# is not in the inference hot path).
TRANSFORMERS_VERSION=5.12.1

# kernels 0.14.1 - exactly v0.5.21's constraint (kernels>=0.14.1,<0.15,
# unchanged). PERF-NEUTRAL on SM121: the only hub-loaded kernel
# (sgl-flash-attn3) is hard-disabled on GB10 and has no sm_121/ARM64 builds.
KERNELS_VERSION=0.14.1

# nvidia-cutlass-dsl 4.6.2 - UNCHANGED, still exactly v0.5.21's pyproject pin
# (nvidia-cutlass-dsl[cu13]==4.6.2). The explicit pin stays mandatory because
# NVIDIA has shipped different wheel CONTENT under the same version number
# before (the 4.5.2 mlir_global_dtors 'data' ICE, see
# reference_cutlass_dsl_wheel_swap).
# Re-verify on the built image with the rmsnorm smoke test from the v0.5.18
# recipe (and confirm the DSL path is actually TAKEN: norm/__init__.py falls
# back to CUDA JIT SILENTLY when the DSL cannot target the arch).
# Fallback: 4.6.1, then 4.6.0.
CUTLASS_DSL_VERSION=4.6.2

# Audio multimodal deps - see the 0.5.15.post1 recipe. SGLang pulls numba itself;
# librosa is still needed (soundfile/audioread).
AUDIO_DEPS="librosa"

# accelerate - baked into the image (ModelOptModelLoader imports it).
ACCELERATE_DEPS="accelerate"

# huggingface_hub FLOOR (not an exact pin), unchanged. Guards against the xet
# gated-repo download bug (hub PR #4394 forwarded the REDACTED xetHash for GATED
# repos to hf_xet -> "Unable to parse string as hex hash value"); fixed by hub
# PR #4595 in v1.26.0. See FIXED_UPSTREAM_HF_XET_BUG.md. Installed as the LAST
# pip action of the builder stage so nothing can downgrade it afterwards.
HF_HUB_MIN_VERSION=1.26.0

# tokenizers 0.22.2 - exactly v0.5.21's pyproject pin, UNCHANGED. The knob is
# still needed: missing_deps.py checks presence and not version, and the late
# transformers step installs with --pre, so pip may otherwise resolve
# 0.23.0rc0 inside transformers' own tokenizers>=0.22.0,<=0.23.0 range.
# Enforced by scripts/patches/dockerfile-tokenizers-pin.patch as the last pip
# action of the builder stage.
TOKENIZERS_VERSION=0.22.2

SGLANG_VERSION=0.5.21
SGLANG_REF="v0.5.21"

# main-ahead sgl-kernel patch variant. Kept at 1 for provenance (the -v0.5.21
# files carry the mainahead content, the mscclpp link refactor is still in the
# tree), but SGL_KERNEL_PATCH_VARIANT takes precedence in apply_patches(), so
# the -mainahead siblings themselves are not used on this ref.
SGL_KERNEL_MAINAHEAD=1

# Suffix of the four CMakeLists source patches to install under the canonical
# names. "-v0.5.21" = the -v0.5.20 edits re-anchored against v0.5.21; the patch
# BODIES are byte-identical, only the hunk line numbers move (#40033 removed
# four csrc/speculative/*.cu entries from the SOURCES list above the
# skip-sm90-target / skip-flashmla regions). All four regenerated with zero
# fuzz and zero offset. The -v0.5.20 set does NOT fail loudly on this ref
# (offset -4), so the suffix is discipline, not a tripwire.
SGL_KERNEL_PATCH_VARIANT="-v0.5.21"

# Where the sgl-kernel tree lives inside the sglang checkout (moved there by RFC
# #29630 in v0.5.17), passed to the Dockerfile as ARG SGL_KERNEL_DIR (default
# "sgl-kernel", so older recipes are byte-identical). UNCHANGED in v0.5.21
# (package version still 0.4.7); MUST match the path in the patch variant above.
SGL_KERNEL_DIR=python/sglang/kernels/aot

# ── CORE SM121 JIT-header patch: TARGET STILL GONE (PR #30448) -> OFF ────────
# nvfp4_blockwise_moe.cuh does not exist anywhere in v0.5.21 (verified
# 2026-10-03) and cutlass_moe_fp4() is still absent; NVFP4 MoE runs through
# FlashInfer-CUTLASS on SM100/SM120/SM121, the backend our model profiles pin
# anyway (moe_runner_backend: flashinfer_cutlass). At 1 the in-container dry-run
# would abort the build. Consequence: see OPEN RISK B.
APPLY_SGL_KERNEL_SM121=0

# ── DeepSeek-V4 FlashMLA kernel: DROPPED (native since v0.5.13) ──────────────
FLASH_MLA_REPO=
FLASH_MLA_REF=
DSV4_KERNEL_REPO=
DSV4_KERNEL_REF=
DSV4_KERNEL_ARCH=

# ── DeepSeek-V4 NVFP4 MoE: NATIVE since v0.5.14 (PR #25820) -> OFF ──────────
APPLY_DSV4_NVFP4_PR25820=0

# ── DeepSeek-V4 EAGLE-MTP marlin branch + TileLang indexer compat -> ON ──────
# Unchanged rationale: HybridFp8NvFp4Config.get_quant_method still has no marlin
# branch for the MTP/nextn draft-MoE layers in v0.5.21 (it goes straight to
# Mxfp4FlashinferTrtllmMoEMethod, verified 2026-10-03), and the TileLang uint8
# arg check still bites. Both source patches dry-run-verified against v0.5.21
# on 2026-10-03 (marlin: offset 282; tilelang: offset 46).
APPLY_DSV4_MTP_MARLIN_TILELANG=1

# Variant of the tilelang compat patch. "-v0.5.16" selects
# sglang-tilelang-018-indexer-compat-v0.5.16.patch: the path introduced by RFC
# #29630 (python/sglang/kernels/ops/attention/dsa/) and only the uint8-view hunk,
# because upstream adopted the 2D alloc_shared half. That file name is a
# GENERATION label, not a ref restriction; the path and the hunk are unchanged
# in v0.5.21, verified applying at offset 46.
TILELANG_PATCH_VARIANT="-v0.5.16"

# ── Qwen3.6 ModelOpt mixed NVFP4: MERGED (PR #27906) -> OFF ─────────────────
# The OPEN dispatch fix #28099 is a RUNTIME patch in sglang_launch.sh and is
# unaffected by this flag (p21/p22); re-check Qwen3.6 live.
APPLY_QWEN36_MIXED_NVFP4_PR27906=0

# ── Qwen4-Exp / Qwen3.8-Flash-Next: NATIVE (PR #37500, since v0.5.20) -> OFF ─
